od","ends":"2026-09-15T21:30:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Mesa, CO; Grand, UT","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.9240c195bbbaffebcf719c01f9691af687ce6bf8.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.9240c195bbbaffebcf719c01f9691af687ce6bf8.001.1"},{"event":"Special Weather Statement","headline":"Special Weather Statement issued September 15 at 6:32PM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"At 632 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm 12\nmiles north of Fruita, or 18 miles northwest of Grand Junction,\nmoving east at 20 mph.\n\nHAZARD...Wind gusts of 50 to 55 mph and half inch hail.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around\nunsecured objects. Minor hail damage to vegetation is\npossible.\n\nThis storm will remain over mainly rural areas of northwestern Mesa\nCounty.","ends":"2026-09-15T19:00:00-06:00","severity":"Moderate","areaDesc":"Roan and Tavaputs Plateaus; Grand Valley","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1c30a46c0a4d80ffb4e827140d8823c0af2678a9.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1c30a46c0a4d80ffb4e827140d8823c0af2678a9.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-09-15T23:41:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 152341 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 541 PM MDT Tue Sep 15 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Cooler weather today. Limited shower and storm chances, mostly over the higher terrain. - Temperatures bounce back tomorrow, but then average near or even slightly below seasonal normals through next weekend. - Unsettled pattern rest of this week. Thursday","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-09-15T21:13:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Tonight and Wednesday... A few isolated showers and storms will be possible over the high terrain this evening, with chances decreasing after midnight. B